<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Domažlice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1431</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Taus · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Domažlice was fought in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> on 14 August 1431, when the fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussites">Hussites</a>, led by Frederick of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and the papal legate Cardinal Giuliano Cesarini, broke up in panic as the Hussite armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prokop-the-great">Prokop the Great</a> approached. Its failure persuaded the Church to negotiate, leading to the talks with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-domazlice.jpg" alt="Battle of Domažlice" width="320" height="116" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikoláš Aleš · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:U_Doma%C5%BElic.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
